 <span class=\"naviSQ\">Setup &gt; Network Setup</span> screen.</li>\r\n175:   </ul>\r\n176:   <h1 id=\"overview\"> <a href=\"#contents\" class=\"contentArrow\">&#9650;</a> Overview </h1>\r\n177:   <center>\r\n178:     <img src=\"overview.png\" width=\"85%\" />\r\n179:   </center>\r\n180:   <br />\r\n181:   <br />\r\n182:   <table>\r\n183:     <tbody>\r\n184:       <tr>\r\n185:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"1.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n186:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Screen menu</u>: <span class=\"naviMP\">Processing</span> shows processing parameters for the selected channel, <span class=\"naviMP\">Routing</span> displays all routing options for each channel, <span class=\"naviMP\">Meters</span> shows metering for all layers channels and the meters RTA, <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> all scene management, <span class=\"naviMP\">Setup</span> shows available SQ and MixPad setup options, <span class=\"naviMP\">IO Patch</span> displays the patching matrix.</p></td>\r\n187:       </tr>\r\n188:       <tr>\r\n189:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"2.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n190:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Library</u>: 'Illuminates' when an associated library is available for the current view.<br />\r\n191:         </p></td>\r\n192:       </tr>\r\n193:       <tr>\r\n194:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"3.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n195:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Connected device</u>: Displays the network name of the connected console. <br />\r\n196:           </p></td>\r\n197:       </tr>\r\n198:       <tr>\r\n199:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"4.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n200:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Session Menu</u>: Logout and Pull (to pull data from the SQ) options. <br />\r\n201:           </p></td>\r\n202:       </tr>\r\n203:       <tr>\r\n204:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"5.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n205:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Selected channel</u>: Displays the name and channel of the current selection (touch to edit channel name/colour).<br />\r\n206:           </p></td>\r\n207:       </tr>\r\n208:       <tr>\r\n209:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"6.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n210:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Processing select</u>: Touch/click on a processing block to display and adjust parameters. In extended processing view,\r\n211:             this is displayed with similar graphics to those on the SQ.</p></td>\r\n212:       </tr>\r\n213:       <tr>\r\n214:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"7.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n215:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Screen split</u>: Touch/click and drag up or down to show either processing <em>and</em> faders (default), extended processing (drag down), or extended faders (drag up).</p></td>\r\n216:       </tr>\r\n217:       <tr>\r\n218:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"8.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n219:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Meters and block selection</u>: Displays the meters for all channel strips on the currently selected layer. Can\r\n220:             also be touched/clicked to jump to a block of strips.</p></td>\r\n221:       </tr>\r\n222:       <tr>\r\n223:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"9.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n224:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Layer select</u>: Touch/click any of the channel types or layers to display channel strips.</p></td>\r\n225:       </tr>\r\n226:       <tr>\r\n227:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"10.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n228:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Standard/Custom/SQ layers</u>: Touch/click to switch between layer types. Extended fader view shows both types and the\r\n229:             button disappears. In extended processing view, this changes to allow a choice between viewing processing or\r\n230:             layers. SQ layers displayed if <span class=\"naviMP\">Use SQ Layers</span> option in <span class=\"naviMP\">Setup &gt; MixPad</span> is turned on.</p></td>\r\n231:       </tr>\r\n232:       <tr>\r\n233:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"11.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n234:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Processing parameters</u>: Touch/click and drag either the graphical display or parameter value boxes to adjust. In the\r\n235:             extended processing view, more parameters and graphics are shown including RTA on the PEQ screen, and histograms on the\r\n236:             gate and compressor screens.</p></td>\r\n237:       </tr>\r\n238:       <tr>\r\n239:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"12.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n240:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Current/Next</u>: The last recalled (current) and next/selected scenes.</p></td>\r\n241:       </tr>\r\n242:       <tr>\r\n243:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"13.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n244:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p><u>PAFL meter</u>: Duplicates the 12-segment meter on the SQ.</p></td>\r\n245:       </tr>\r\n246:       <tr>\r\n247:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"14.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n248:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p><u>Mix select</u>: Touch/click any mix button to show sends on faders and the master strip for that mix.</p></td>\r\n249:       </tr>\r\n250: \t\t      <tr>\r\n251:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"15.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n252:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Channel strip</u>: As standard, this displays name, mute, send to selected mix, level metering, compressor level\r\n253:             reduction, gate activity and PAFL button. Extended processing view minimises channels to selection only, and when\r\n254:             selected displays them in place of the master strip. Extended fader view displays assignment and pan options. Touch/click\r\n255:             any channel to select it. The selected channel is highlighted in green.</p></td>\r\n256:       </tr>\r\n257: \r\n258:       <tr>\r\n259:         <td class=\"tableNumbers\"><img src=\"16.png\" class=\"numberImage\" /></td>\r\n260:         <td class=\"tableText\"><p> <u>Master strip</u>: Displays the master send for the selected mix. Can be selected in the same way as other channels\r\n261:             to adjust output processing.</p></td>\r\n262:       </tr>\r\n263:     </tbody>\r\n264:   </table>\r\n265:   <h1 id=\"using\"> <a href=\"#contents\" class=\"contentArrow\">&#9650;</a> Using the app connected to an SQ</h1>\r\n266:   <p>SQ MixPad sends and receives control messages to and from the SQ. It does not transmit or receive audio. Please refer to\r\n267:     the reference guide for details on the firmware you are controlling.</p>\r\n268:   <p>When logging on, SQ MixPad receives all the settings of the SQ. To synchronise correctly, MixPad should be connected after\r\n269:     the initial setup of the mixer, and after all remote audio units have been connected.</p>\r\n270:   <p>Workflow is the same as on the SQ itself:</p>\r\n271:   <ul>\r\n272:     <li>Select a mix  to show and adjust send levels with faders.</li>\r\n273:     <li>Select a layer, followed by a channel  then select a processing block  to view and make adjustments to the selected channel.</li>\r\n274:   </ul>\r\n275:   <p> <span class=\"info\">Note</span> - SQ MixPad adheres to SQ User Permissions and blocked parameters or mixes will either be\r\n276:     'greyed-out' or display a pop-up when touched/clicked. To access the SQ using the SQ MixPad app, the user logging on must have the\r\n277:     MixPad option set to 'Allow' in their user permissions.</p>\r\n278:   <h3>Setup, custom layers/SQ layers and navigation</h3>\r\n279:   <p>There are 6 'Standard' layers - Inputs, Mix, FX, DCA's, Mute Groups and SoftKeys which are always available.</p>\r\n280:   <p>There are also 6 <span class=\"naviMP\">Custom</span> layers which can be customised for each instance of MixPad for different operators e.g. a separate Monitor or Broadcast engineer.</p>\r\n281:   <p>Alternatively,  the SQ (hardware) layers can be mirrored and used in place of the custom layers by turning on the <span class=\"naviMP\">Use SQ Layers</span> option in <span class=\"naviMP\">Setup  &gt; MixPad &gt; Banks</span>.<br>\r\n282:   (<span class=\"info\">Note</span> - This works in one direction, the desk cannot follow the custom layers in MixPad and it is only possible to setup the SQ layers on the desk itself or when editing a show offline). </p>\r\n283:   <p>To set which channels appear in the custom layers:</p>\r\n284:   <ul>\r\n285:     <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Setup</span> screen, and select <span class=\"naviMP\">Custom Strip</span>.</li>\r\n286:     <li>Touch/click options on the top bar to view different channel types.</li>\r\n287:     <li>Touch/click a channel or drag and drop from top to bottom to assign it to the layer.</li>\r\n288:     <li>Drag from bottom to top to unassign.</li>\r\n289:     <li>Drag and drop in the bottom to reorder.</li>\r\n290:     <li>Touch/click the <span class=\"naviMP\">Clear</span> button to clear the layer.</li>\r\n291:     <li>Drag and drop a <span class=\"naviMP\">Blank</span> to add a spacer.</li>\r\n292:     <li>Touch/click <span class=\"naviMP\">Copy Desk Layer</span> to copy a layer from the SQ.</li>\r\n293:   </ul>\r\n294:   <p>The <span class=\"naviMP\">MixPad</span> section in the <span class=\"naviMP\">Setup</span> screen shows  MixPad device settings:</p>\r\n295:   <ul>\r\n296:     <li> <span class=\"naviMP\">Lock Bank Scrolling</span> - If this is on, it disables swiping left and right on faders to view other\r\n297:       channels in the layer. You can continue to touch/click the metering blocks (above the faders) to navigate.</li>\r\n298:     <li> <span class=\"naviMP\">Visible channels in bank</span> - You can choose to view 8, 12 or 16 channels at once.</li>\r\n299:     <li> <span class=\"naviMP\">Follow SQ Mix Select</span> - With this option On, MixPad will follow mix selection on the SQ surface<br>\r\n300:       (<span class=\"info\">Note</span> - This works in one direction, the desk cannot follow the mix selected in MixPad). <br />\r\n301:     </li>\r\n302:     <li> <span class=\"naviMP\">Follow SQ Channel Select</span> - With this option On, MixPad will follow channel selection on the SQ\r\n303:       surface<br>\r\n304:       (<span class=\"info\">Note</span> - This works in one direction, the desk cannot follow the channel selected in MixPad).</li>\r\n305:     <li> <span class=\"naviMP\">Display Mix Names</span> - With this option On, the Mix name will display on the right of the\r\n306:       processing screen. Set Off to display the mix number instead.</li>\r\n307:     <li> <span class=\"naviMP\">Show Demo Metering</span> - This option switches the demo metering in offline mode either On or Off.</li>\r\n308:     <li><span class=\"naviMP\">IO Patch Safe Button</span> - When On, safe patching with the 'Patch' switch is active in the<span class=\"naviMP\"> IO Patch</span> screen. When Off, the switch does not appear and you can always patch.</li>\r\n309:   </ul>\r\n310:   <p>Additional settings in offline mode:</p>\r\n311:   <ul>\r\n312:     <li><span class=\"naviMP\">SQ Model</span> - Select the  SQ model that the offline mode will use, this affects the number of strips that can be assigned to a layer, and the number of local input and output sockets available.</li>\r\n313:   </ul>\r\n314:   <p>Additional settings on Windows or Mac:</p>\r\n315:   <ul>\r\n316:     <li><span class=\"naviMP\">Copy, Paste and Reset Menu</span> - This gives the option of either using a Right Click or Double Tap (Double Click) to open the Copy, Paste and Reset pop-up.</li>\r\n317:   </ul>\r\n318:   <h3>Adjusting levels and processing parameters</h3>\r\n319:   <p>To make adjustments to processing parameters, select a processing block (i.e. Preamp, Gate, PEQ or Compressor on an\r\n320:     input channel). Then touch/click and drag points on the processing graphic, or values in the parameter boxes to adjust.</p>\r\n321:   <ul>\r\n322:     <li>When controlling PEQ, bandwidth can be controlled using the slide control or a 'pinch' gesture.</li>\r\n323:     <li>Drag down the horizontal centre divide (which shows all channel meters for the current layer) to display more parameters. This includes channel naming and colour selection on\r\n324:       the preamp screen, and HPF when on the PEQ screen.</li>\r\n325:   </ul>\r\n326:   <h3>Fine adjustment</h3>\r\n327:   <p>When adjusting any parameter (including fader levels), control works on two axis. One axis increases or decreases the\r\n328:     value, whilst the other axis adjusts how fine the control is. Moving further away from the control allows smaller adjustments\r\n329:     to be made.</p>\r\n330:   <p>For example, touch/click and drag a fader up and down to change the send level. If you then keep the fader selected but\r\n331:     move to the left or right, you will notice that the same up and down movement will make less of a change. </p>\r\n332:   <center>\r\n333:     <img src=\"fineAdjust.png\" width=\"60%\"/>\r\n334:   </center>\r\n335:   <h3>Copy, Paste and Reset </h3>\r\n336:   <p>Open the Copy, Paste, Reset pop-up in MixPad by either double tapping  or right clicking (optional on Windows/Mac) on a processing graphic or channel name/fader.</p>\r\n337:   <p>As with the SQ, individual processing blocks or whole channel processing can be copied, along with assignments and send levels of mixes.</p>\r\n338:   <h3>Libraries</h3>\r\n339:   <p> The <span class=\"naviMP\">Lib</span> button to the left of the screen menu illuminates whenever a library is available for the  visible processing. Selecting this will open the library pop-up, allowing presets to be stored and recalled.</p>\r\n340:   <p><span class=\"info\">Notes</span> -</p>\r\n341:   <ul>\r\n342:     <li>When opening any input channel processing library, a second tab 'Input Channel' can be selected, select this to manage full  channel presets.</li>\r\n343:     <li>Libraries are  used to recall different RackFX units. The FX library can be opened when either an FX Send or FX Return channel is selected.</li></ul>\r\n344:   <h3>Meters and 'PAFL' RTA</h3>\r\n345:   <ul>\r\n346:     <li>Touch/click <span class=\"naviMP\">Meters</span> then select a layer or channel type on the left to show metering for that layer or channel type. Level, Mute/PAFL\r\n347:       status, Gate activity and Gain reduction are displayed.</li>\r\n348:     <li>Touch/click the <span class=\"naviMP\">RTA</span> button on the left of the meters screen to show the RTA.</li>\r\n349:     <li>This is the same RTA as shown on the SQ <span class=\"naviSQ\">Meters</span> screen, and all source and parameter settings are shared.</li>\r\n350:     <li>The meters RTA can be set to follow the PAFL selection and as there is one PAFL bus,  pressing the PAFL button on a channel in MixPad will also action the same channel's PAFL on the SQ.</li>\r\n351:     <li>The RTA displays the level of each frequency band and denotes the most prominent frequency in red.  </li>\r\n352:   </ul>\r\n353:   <h3>PEQ and GEQ RTA</h3>\r\n354:   <ul>\r\n355:     <li>When viewing either PEQ or GEQ  on the <span class=\"naviMP\">Processing</span> screen, drag the horizontal centre divide down to display extended processing.When viewing GEQ, the RTA settings will be shown automatically. When viewing PEQ, touch/click the <span class=\"naviMP\">RTA</span> button to the right of the PEQ parameters to display RTA settings.</li>\r\n356:     <li>The RTA displays the level of each frequency band and denotes the most prominent frequency in red whenever bars are used.</li>\r\n357:     <li>The RTA displayed on PEQ and GEQ processing screens is the same as that shown on the console, if 'Follow Device' is active on multiple devices, other users may 'steal' the RTA.</li>\r\n358:     <li>If the RTA for a different channel is being  displayed through use of the &lsquo;<strong>Fixed Channel</strong>&rsquo; option, the RTA source is  shown at the top right.</li>\r\n359:     <li>If the RTA for a different channel is displayed  because it has been selected by the SQ or another instance of SQ-MixPad, the RTA source is shown at the top  right with a &lsquo;!&rsquo; prefix and the RTA meters will  be greyed out.</li>\r\n360:     <li>Stereo sources display metering for left and right channels summed.</li>\r\n361:     <li>Touch the <strong class=\"naviMP\">PEQ</strong> button to return to the  PEQ settings when in the PEQ screen.  </li>\r\n362:   </ul>\r\n363:   <h3>Patching</h3>\r\n364:   <ul>\r\n365:     <li>Touch/click <span class=\"naviMP\">IO Patch</span> to display the patching matrix.</li>\r\n366:     <li>Touch/click and drag to move around the matrix and zoom in or out by using a 'pinch' gesture on a touchscreen device, or a\r\n367:       scroll wheel if using a mouse.</li>\r\n368:     <li>Touck/click the <span class=\"naviMP\">Patch</span> button at the top left of the patching matrix to allow patching.</li>\r\n369:     <li>With patching enabled, touch/click any matrix box to create or remove a patch.</li>\r\n370:     <li>To block patch diagonally, touch/click and hold until the patch block is highlighted in blue, then drag diagonally and release to create the patch.</li>\r\n371:   </ul>\r\n372:   <p> <span class=\"info\">Notes</span> -</p>\r\n373:   <ul>\r\n374:     <li>When patching inputs, input sources are displayed at the top and destination channels in the SQ are displayed on the\r\n375:     left.</li>\r\n376:     <li>When patching outputs, SQ channel sources are displayed on the left and output sockets and destinations are displayed\r\n377:       at the top.</li>\r\n378:     <li>When patching tie lines, inputs are displayed on the left and outputs are displayed at the top.</li>\r\n379:   </ul>\r\n380:   <h3>Online data management </h3>\r\n381:       <p> When connected to a console, MixPad is accessing scenes and libraries which are stored in the SQ.</p>\r\n382: <p> <span class=\"info\">Note</span> - Refer to the SQ Reference Manual to see the parameters and settings stored variously at desk, show and scene levels.  </p>\r\n383: <h3>Scene management</h3>\r\n384:   <p><u>To store a new scene:</u></p>\r\n385:       <ol>\r\n386:         <li>Adjust scene level parameters</li>\r\n387:         <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> screen and select an empty scene slot</li>\r\n388:         <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Store</span> button to store the scene with a default name, or touch/click in the edit name box to name the scene as it's stored</li>\r\n389:       </ol>\r\n390:       <p><span class=\"info\">Notes</span> - </p>\r\n391:       <ul>\r\n392:         <li>It is possible to use Copy, Paste and Reset directly on the scene slots in the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes &gt; Scene Manager</span> screen.</li>\r\n393:         <li>With a scene selected, touch/click the edit name box to rename at any time.</li>\r\n394:       </ul>\r\n395:       <p><u>To recall a scene:</u></p>\r\n396:       <ol>\r\n397:         <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> screen and select a scene</li>\r\n398:         <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Recall</span> button to recall the scene</li>\r\n399:       </ol>\r\n400:   <p><u>To set scene recall filters:</u></p>\r\n401:       <ol>\r\n402:         <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> screen and select a stored scene</li>\r\n403:         <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Recall Filter</span> button to show the scene filter pop-up</li>\r\n404:         <li>Use filter buttons to allow or block parameter changes when recalling the selected scene.</li>\r\n405:       </ol>\r\n406:       <p><span class=\"info\">Note</span> - When storing scenes, all parameters are stored, filters affect only whether or not they are recalled.</p>\r\n407:       <p><u>To edit a scene:</u></p>\r\n408:   <ol>\r\n409:         <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> screen and select the scene you wish to edit</li>\r\n410:         <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Recall</span> button to recall the scene</li>\r\n411:         <li>Adjust parameters in the <span class=\"naviMP\">Processing</span> screen</li>\r\n412:         <li>Return to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> screen</li>\r\n413:         <li>Ensure the same scene is selected</li>\r\n414:         <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Store</span> button and when prompted, agree to overwrite the scene  </li>\r\n415:   </ol>\r\n416:   <h3>Library management</h3>\r\n417:       <p><u>To store a library preset:</u></p>\r\n418:       <ol>\r\n419:         <li>Adjust processing for either a whole channel or a particular processing 'block' (or set input channel patching)</li>\r\n420:         <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Lib</span> button to show the library pop-up (when opening any input channel processing library, a second tab is available to manage full input channel presets)</li>\r\n421:         <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Store New </span>or <span class=\"naviMP\">Overwrite</span> buttons to store the preset</li>\r\n422:       </ol>\r\n423:       <p><u>To recall a  preset:</u></p>\r\n424:       <ol>\r\n425:         <li>Go to the processing section where you want the preset to be recalled</li>\r\n426:         <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Lib</span> button to show the library pop-up (when opening any input channel processing library, a second tab is available to manage full input channel presets)</li>\r\n427:         <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Factory</span>/<span class=\"naviMP\">User</span> switch to see Factory or User presets</li>\r\n428:         <li>Select a preset and use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Recall</span> button to recall it</li>\r\n429:       </ol>\r\n430:       <p><span class=\"info\">Notes</span> - </p>\r\n431:       <ul>\r\n432:         <li>When recalling Input Channel Library presets, you can choose whether to recall Preamp, Name and Colour using buttons on the left.</li>\r\n433:         <li>Library presets are stored within the show, but can also be stored individually to a USB storage device from the console, or when in MixPad's Offline mode to either the mobile device's storage or the working directory.</li>\r\n434:       </ul>\r\n435:     </li>\r\n436:   </ul>\r\n437:   <h1 id=\"offline\"> <a href=\"#contents\" class=\"contentArrow\">&#9650;</a> Offline mode </h1>\r\n438:   <p>MixPad's offline mode allows you to edit  parameters and manage the scenes of a show when not connected to an\r\n439:     SQ. It also allows you to manage multiple shows easily and can send (push) and receive (pull) shows through the SQ's network\r\n440:     connection.</p>\r\n441:   <p>You can enter offline mode by selecting <span class=\"naviMP\">Offline</span> from the <span class=\"naviMP\">Choose Unit</span> list when starting the app. The option to switch to offline mode is also presented\r\n442:     immediately after pulling a show from an SQ.</p>\r\n443:   <p>To Push or Pull shows, you must ensure the correct SQ User Permissions have been allowed. These are found in the SQ <span class=\"naviSQ\">Setup &gt; Users &gt; Setup Permissions</span> screen as <span class=\"naviSQ\">Sync Push</span> and <span class=\"naviSQ\">Sync Pull</span>.</p>\r\n444:   <p><span class=\"info\">Note</span> - In order to transfer an entire show to or from SQ-MixPad, any other remote devices will be disconnected once the transfer begins. Devices can  be reconnected once the transfer is complete.</p>\r\n445:   <h3>Starting with a template/default show </h3>\r\n446:   <ol>\r\n447:     <li>Go to <span class=\"naviMP\">Utility &gt; Shows</span> and touch/click <span class=\"naviMP\">New...</span>.</li>\r\n448:     <li>Select the template for the SQ model you will be using. Template shows have no scenes and contain exactly the\r\n449:       same settings as when you perform a hard reset on the SQ.</li>\r\n450:   </ol>\r\n451:   <p> <span class=\"info\">Notes</span> -</p>\r\n452:   <ul>\r\n453:     <li>With a new install of SQ MixPad, opening offline mode will load the SQ-7 template show.</li>\r\n454:     <li>As a MixPad template show includes the default settings for <u>all</u> show parameters in the SQ (including those that cannot be edited with MixPad), pushing a show that was started\r\n455:       as a MixPad template will reset all unedited SQ parameters to default, for example, the surface LED/brightness settings. If\r\n456:       you have a non-default SQ setup that you often use, it is best to set this up on the SQ first, then pull it to MixPad and\r\n457:       save it as a local show for use as your personal template. <br />\r\n458:     </li>\r\n459:   </ul>\r\n460:   <h3>Pulling a show (SQ to MixPad) </h3>\r\n461:   <ol>\r\n462:     <li>In online or offline mode, go to the session menu in the top left corner and select <span class=\"naviMP\">Pull Show</span></li>\r\n463:     <li>On the SQ, go to the <span class=\"naviSQ\">Utility &gt; Data &gt; Sync</span> screen, touch the <span class=\"naviSQ\">Sync Mode</span> button and follow on screen instructions to enter sync mode.<br>\r\n464:     </li>\r\n465:     <li>The entire show from the SQ will then be pulled to MixPad's offline mode.</li>\r\n466:     <li>You are now given the option to immediately store the show you have pulled. You do not have to store the show separately, but this is best practice and will enable you to return to it later if required.</li>\r\n467:     <li>Offline mode will now contain the show that was pulled from the SQ for editing.</li>\r\n468:   </ol>\r\n469:   <p> <span class=\"info\">Notes</span> - </p>\r\n470:   <ul>\r\n471:     <li>When a show is 'pulled' from the SQ, the show loaded in MixPad's offline mode will be completely overwritten, so it is\r\n472:       important to save any offline changes you have made <u>before</u> pulling a show.</li>\r\n473:     <li>Like the SQ, MixPad can load one show at a time. However, multiple shows can be stored locally on each MixPad\r\n474:       device or in the working directory.</li>\r\n475:     <li>MixPad pulls <u>all</u> show data, so it is best practice to pull a show with your standard settings, which can then be stored and used\r\n476:       as your personal template.</li>\r\n477:     <li>Sync mode  connects to  one device at a time, other device will be disconnected to ensure data is transferred correctly and devices will not be able to reconnect until transfer is complete.</li>\r\n478:   </ul>\r\n479:   <h3>Pushing a show (MixPad to SQ) </h3>\r\n480:   <ol>\r\n481:     <li>In offline mode, go to the session menu in the top left corner and select <span class=\"naviMP\">Push Show</span> or <span class=\"naviMP\">Push Show To...</span></li>\r\n482:     <li>If selecting <span class=\"naviMP\">Push Show</span> you will now see the <span class=\"naviMP\">Choose Unit</span> list where you can select the SQ you are wanting to push the show to. Selecting <span class=\"naviMP\">Push Show To...</span> will bypass the list and select the last SQ that was connected.</li>\r\n483:     <li>On the SQ, go to the <span class=\"naviSQ\">Utility &gt; Data &gt; Sync</span> screen, touch the <span class=\"naviSQ\">Sync Mode</span> button and follow on screen instructions to enter sync mode.<br>\r\n484:     </li>\r\n485:     <li>The entire show currently loaded in SQ MixPad's offline mode will then be pushed to the SQ.</li>\r\n486:   </ol>\r\n487:   <p> <span class=\"info\">Notes</span> - </p>\r\n488:   <ul>\r\n489:     <li>When a show is 'pushed' to the SQ, the show currently loaded in the SQ will be completely overwritten, so it is\r\n490:       important to store any changes you have made on the desk to a USB device <u>before</u> pushing a show. <br />\r\n491:     </li>\r\n492:     <li>As a MixPad show includes the settings for <u>all</u> show parameters (including those that cannot be edited with MixPad), all unedited parameters will also be overwritten, for example, the surface LED/brightness settings. If you have a non-default SQ setup that you often use, it is best to set this up on the SQ first, then pull it to MixPad and save it as a local show for use as your personal template. </li>\r\n493:     <li>Sync mode  connects to  one device at a time, other device will be disconnected to ensure data is transferred correctly and will not be able to reconnect until transfer is complete.</li>\r\n494:   </ul>\r\n495:   <h3>Channel Strip Layers </h3>\r\n496:   <p>Instead of the custom layers which exist in online mode, offline mode instead shows layers A-F which match the desk layers. This allows the layout of the SQ channel strips for each show/scene to be setup when offline. The process for this is exactly the same as for setting up MixPad custom layers in online mode (described in the online setup section above).</p>\r\n497:   <h3>Adjusting parameters </h3>\r\n498:   <p> All offline parameters are adjusted in exactly the same way as when online, but instead of making live changes to the SQ, they make changes to the offline state. The offline state can then be stored to an offline scene in the offline show, and the offline show can then be stored, recalled, shared or pushed to the SQ.</p>\r\n499:   <h3>Libraries</h3>\r\n500:   <p> The <span class=\"naviMP\">Lib</span> button to the left of the screen menu illuminates whenever a library is available for the  visible processing. Selecting this will open the library pop-up allowing presets to be stored and recalled.</p>\r\n501:   <p><span class=\"info\">Notes</span> -</p>\r\n502:   <ul>\r\n503:     <li>When opening any input channel processing library, a second tab is available to manage full input channel presets.</li>\r\n504:     <li>As on the SQ console, libraries are also used to recall different RackFX units. The FX library can be opened when either an FX Send or FX Return channel is selected.</li>\r\n505:     <li>Library presets are stored locally (within the show), but individual library presets can be imported (<span class=\"naviMP\">&lt; To Local</span>) and exported (<span class=\"naviMP\">To Working &gt;</span>) in the <span class=\"naviMP\">Utility &gt; Libraries</span> screen.</li>\r\n506:   </ul>\r\n507:   <h3>Changing the SQ model</h3>\r\n508:   <p> Some settings are model dependent, such as the available local sockets and the maximum number of strips that can be added to a layer. Therefore, if setting up for the first time, or when converting a show from one model to another, it is  best to select the correct SQ model you will be using. This is done in the <span class=\"naviMP\">Setup &gt; MixPad</span> screen, in the <span class=\"naviMP\">Offline</span> section.</p>\r\n509:   <h3>Offline data management </h3>\r\n510:   <p> MixPad's offline mode behaves in the same way as the SQ:</p>\r\n511:   <ul>\r\n512:     <li>One show can be loaded at a time. This contains all show level settings and up to 300 scenes.</li>\r\n513:     <li>There is only one current 'state', which is the one being adjusted, and this can be stored to a scene.</li>\r\n514:     <li>Recalling a scene will overwrite the current state with the contents of the  scene being recalled, adjustments can then be made and the scene can be stored again.</li>\r\n515:   </ul>\r\n516:   <p>When using a mobile device, data is stored and recalled from the device memory. Manually deleting or uninstalling the app will therefore delete all stored data.</p>\r\n517:   <p>If a PC (Windows or Mac) is being used, you must set a working directory at the bottom of the <span class=\"naviMP\">Utility &gt; Shows</span> screen.\r\n518:   To work with shows on a USB device that has been formatted in the SQ, this should be set to '<strong>[USB Drive]:/AHSQ</strong>'.</p>\r\n519:     <center>\r\n520:     <img src=\"workingDirectory.png\" width=\"50%\" />\r\n521:   </center>\r\n522:   <p>This means shows, scenes and libraries can  be stored on the USB device and used directly with the SQ later.</p>\r\n523:   <p>If the correct folder structure does not already exist in the chosen Working Directory, MixPad will ask to create the SHOWS, SCENES and LIBRARY folders in the location chosen.</p>\r\n524:   <p> <span class=\"info\">Note</span> - Refer to the SQ Reference Manual to see the parameters and settings stored variously at desk, show and scene levels.</p>\r\n525:   <h3>Scene management</h3>\r\n526:   <p><u>To store a new scene:</u></p>\r\n527:   <ol>\r\n528:     <li>Adjust scene level parameters e.g. processing, levels patching and channel naming.</li>\r\n529:     <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> screen and select an empty scene slot.</li>\r\n530:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Store</span> button to store the scene with a default name, or touch/click in the edit name box to name the scene as it's stored.</li>\r\n531:   </ol>\r\n532:   <p><span class=\"info\">Notes</span> - </p>\r\n533:   <ul>\r\n534:     <li>It is possible to use Copy, Paste and Reset directly on the scene slots in the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes &gt; Scene Manager</span> screen.</li>\r\n535:     <li>With a scene selected, touch/click the edit name box to rename at any time.</li>\r\n536:   </ul>\r\n537:   <p><u>To recall a scene:</u></p>\r\n538:   <ol>\r\n539:     <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> screen and select a scene.</li>\r\n540:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Recall</span> button to recall the scene.</li>\r\n541:   </ol>\r\n542:   <p><u>To set scene filters:</u></p>\r\n543:   <ol>\r\n544:     <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> screen and select a stored scene.</li>\r\n545:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Recall Filter</span> button to show the scene filter pop-up.</li>\r\n546:     <li>Use filter buttons to allow or block parameter changes when recalling the selected scene.</li>\r\n547:   </ol>\r\n548:   <p><span class=\"info\">Note</span> - When storing scenes, all parameters are stored, filters affect only whether or not they are recalled.</p>\r\n549:   <p><u>To edit a scene:</u></p>\r\n550:   <ol>\r\n551:     <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> screen and select the scene you wish to edit.</li>\r\n552:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Recall</span> button to recall the scene.</li>\r\n553:     <li>Adjust parameters in the <span class=\"naviMP\">Processing</span> screen.</li>\r\n554:     <li>Return to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Scenes</span> screen.</li>\r\n555:     <li>Ensure the same scene is selected.</li>\r\n556:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Store</span> button and when prompted, agree to overwrite the scene.</li>\r\n557:   </ol>\r\n558:   <h3>Show management </h3>\r\n559:   <p><u>To store a new show:</u></p>\r\n560:   <ol>\r\n561:     <li>Adjust all show level settings and store scenes for the show.</li>\r\n562:     <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Utility &gt; Shows</span> screen.</li>\r\n563:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Store New</span> button to store the entire show.</li>\r\n564:   </ol>\r\n565:   <p><u>To recall a show:</u></p>\r\n566:   <ol>\r\n567:     <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Utility &gt; Shows</span> screen and select a show.</li>\r\n568:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Recall</span> button to recall the entire show and all scenes.</li>\r\n569:   </ol>\r\n570:   <p><u>To edit a show:</u></p>\r\n571:   <ol>\r\n572:     <li>Go to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Utility &gt; Shows</span> screen and select the show you wish to edit.</li>\r\n573:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Recall</span> button to recall the show.</li>\r\n574:     <li>Adjust all show level settings and scenes.</li>\r\n575:     <li>Return to the <span class=\"naviMP\">Utility &gt; Shows</span> screen.</li>\r\n576:     <li>Ensure the same show is selected.</li>\r\n577:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Overwrite</span> button and when prompted, agree to overwrite the show.</li>\r\n578:   </ol>\r\n579:   <h3>Library management</h3>\r\n580:   <p><u>To store a library preset:</u></p>\r\n581:   <ol>\r\n582:     <li>Adjust processing for either a whole channel or a particular processing 'block' (or set input channel patching).</li>\r\n583:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Lib</span> button to show the library pop-up (when opening any input channel processing library, a second tab is available to manage full input channel presets).</li>\r\n584:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Store New </span>or <span class=\"naviMP\">Overwrite</span> buttons to store the preset.</li>\r\n585:   </ol>\r\n586:   <p><u>To recall a  preset:</u></p>\r\n587:   <ol>\r\n588:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Lib</span> button to show the library pop-up (when opening any input channel processing library, a second tab is available to manage full input channel presets).</li>\r\n589:     <li>Use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Factory</span>/<span class=\"naviMP\">User</span> switch to see Factory or User presets.</li>\r\n590:     <li>Select a preset and use the <span class=\"naviMP\">Recall</span> button to recall it.</li>\r\n591:   </ol>\r\n592:   <p><span class=\"info\">Notes</span> - </p>\r\n593:   <ul>\r\n594:     <li>When recalling Input Channel Library presets, you can choose whether to recall Preamp, Name and Colour using buttons on the left.</li>\r\n595:     <li>Library presets are stored locally (within the show), but individual library presets can be imported (<span class=\"naviMP\">&lt; To Local</span>) and exported (<span class=\"naviMP\">To Working &gt;</span>) in the <span class=\"naviMP\">Utility &gt; Libraries</span> screen.</li>\r\n596:   </ul>\r\n597:   <p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n598:   <h1 id=\"troubleshooting\"> <a href=\"#contents\" class=\"contentArrow\">&#9650;</a> Troubleshooting </h1>\r\n599:   <h3>\"The app failed to connect, and it's the latest version\"</h3>\r\n600:   <p>Ensure that the version of the app you are running and the firmware version of the SQ have the same two numbers at the\r\n601:     start (the last number does not need to match). If your app is automatically updated, you may need to update your SQ firmware\r\n602:     to match. <br />\r\n603:   </p>\r\n604:   <h3>\"I cannot see my SQ in the list when starting SQ MixPad\"</h3>\r\n605:   <ul>\r\n606:     <li>Check that the <strong>Lnk</strong> activity light is flashing on the SQ network socket, if not, test all connections and cables.</li>\r\n607:     <li>Check to see that the SQ has an IP address. Go to the <"}
